#. The hint (see the copies line above) for the mouth gene, which every
#. daughter always wears. The row may be shared with a level and a gauge.
#. Room: at most 430 px in 14 px type; the English takes 263 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "the mouth · a daughter always wears it"
msgstr ""

#. The hint under an empty place on the body: nothing is there, so nothing can
#. be passed on to a daughter from it.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type; the English takes 301 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "an empty slot · nothing to pass on from here"
msgstr ""

#. The hint while the player is about to write a waiting gene over one that is
#. already in the DNA. %s is the short word of the gene that would be lost
#. (such as `eat` or `ping`): keep %s as it is. "Your body keeps it" means
#. this cell keeps the organ for the rest of its life, though its daughters
#. will not inherit it. The row is 560 px wide, with a word in place of %s.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 293 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s leaves your dna · your body keeps it"
msgstr ""

#. The same hint for a gene the DNA carries but the body does not wear, so
#. there is no second half. %s is the gene's short word.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 157 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s leaves your dna"
msgstr ""

#. As the hint above, for a gene that has a level (it grows with use). The
#. first %s is the gene's short word, the %d the level. Keep both, in this
#. order.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. 99 in place of the placeholders; the English takes 355 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s leaves your dna · level %d ends with this body"
msgstr ""

#. Same, for a levelled gene the body does not wear. %s is the gene's short
#. word, %d the level.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. 99 in place of the placeholders; the English takes 282 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s leaves your dna · its level %d is lost"
msgstr ""

#. A gene's level, a whole number that grows with use: "level 7". Keep %d.
#. Shown in 14 px type at the start of the hint row, before a gauge and the
#. hint itself, which share the row's 560 px with it.
#. Room: at most 70 px in 14 px type, measured with 99 in place of the
#. placeholders; the English takes 52 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "level %d"
msgstr ""

#. All the `ACT_` lines are one line of instructions in 14 px type, centred
#. under the figure, telling the player what the next tap or release will do.
#. A "slot" is one of seven places round the cell's body where a gene sits;
#. "place" a gene means put it in a slot; "your daughters may wear it" means
#. the cells this one divides into may show the gene as an organ. The row is
#. 560 px wide. This one: a gene is waiting, none is chosen.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type; the English takes 261 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "tap a slot · your daughters may wear it"
msgstr ""

#. A slot is chosen for the waiting gene; a second tap confirms.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type; the English takes 120 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "tap again to place"
msgstr ""

#. The two %s are the short words of two genes, such as `eat` and `ping`: the
#. first is the waiting gene, the second the gene it would replace in the DNA.
#. Keep both %s, in this order.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. your second widest in place of the placeholders; the English takes 249 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "tap again to write %s over %s"
msgstr ""

#. While the player drags a waiting gene over an empty slot; letting go places
#. it there. %s is the gene's short word, such as `eat`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 180 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to place %s here"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a waiting gene over a slot that already holds a gene:
#. letting go only selects it, and a second tap writes over it. The two %s are
#. short gene words: the one being dragged, then the one it would replace.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. your second widest in place of the placeholders; the English takes 330 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go, then tap again to place %s over %s"
msgstr ""

#. Under a gene that is already in a slot: it can be dragged to another slot.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type; the English takes 148 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "drag it to another slot"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a gene that is not over any slot. %s is its short word, such
#. as `eat`; "put it there" means into a slot.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 267 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "%s · let go over a slot to put it there"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a gene over an empty slot of the body. %s is its short word.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 181 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to move %s here"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a gene over a slot that holds another: letting go swaps
#. them. The two %s are the two genes' short words.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word and
#. your second widest in place of the placeholders; the English takes 220 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to swap %s and %s"
msgstr ""

#. While dragging a gene back over the slot it came from: letting go cancels
#. the move. %s is the gene's short word.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 218 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "let go to leave %s where it is"
msgstr ""

#. For a gene that can grow in two different ways (the player picks one, for
#. good). %s is the gene's short word, such as `beam`.
#. Room: at most 560 px in 14 px type, measured with your widest gene word in
#. place of the placeholders; the English takes 259 px.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
#, c-format
msgid "tap again to choose how %s grows"
msgstr ""

