#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "carried"
msgstr ""

#. All eight `LINE_` strings are one-line notices in 18 px type over the
#. water, a few seconds each, in a game shared with a friend. "Their" and
#. "they" are the friend; "water" is the game world (a pond) that one of the
#. two phones hosts. About 50 characters at most. This one: the player has
#. just joined the friend's world.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "you are in their water"
msgstr ""

#. The friend has just joined the player's own world.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "they are in your water"
msgstr ""

#. The friend's cell died; it comes back (is reborn) near the player.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "they died · they come back near you"
msgstr ""

#. The player's cell ate the friend's cell; it comes back (is reborn) near the
#. player.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "you ate them · they come back near you"
msgstr ""

#. The friend's phone has stopped sending anything for a few seconds (screen
#. off, in a pocket, or a bad connection).
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "their phone went quiet"
msgstr ""

#. The friend's world has ended (they left it), and the player carries on in
#. their own world instead.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "their water is gone · this one is yours"
msgstr ""

#. As the line above, but the friend's phone ended the connection because of a
#. fault, rather than the friend leaving: the player carries on in their own
#. world.
#: game/normal/normal_mode.gd
msgid "cut off from their water · this one is yours"
msgstr ""

